# Infinite scroll

Loads the first page of todos, then the next page whenever the visitor
scrolls to the bottom, until the server answers an empty page.

Import Shared.

## Page /

State:
    Let todos be a new Seq of Todo.
    Let error be "".
    Let pageNum be 1.
    Let exhausted be false.
    Let loadedCount always be length of todos.

Actions:
    When the page loads:
        Get "/api/todos?page=1" as Seq of Todo, then loaded.

    To loaded (answer: Result of Seq of Todo and HttpError):
        Inspect answer:
            When Ok (list):
                Let mutable merged be todos.
                Repeat for t in list:
                    Push t to merged.
                Set todos to merged.
                Set error to "".
                If length of list is equal to 0:
                    Set exhausted to true.
            When Err (e):
                Set error to e's message.
                Set exhausted to true.

    When the user scrolls to the bottom:
        If exhausted is equal to false:
            Set pageNum to pageNum + 1.
            Get "/api/todos?page={pageNum}" as Seq of Todo, then loaded.

View:
    <main class="card">
      <h1>Todos <small id="count">({loadedCount})</small></h1>
      {if error is not "":}<p class="error" role="alert">{error}</p>{end}
      <ul class="todos">
        {for each t in todos, keyed by t's id:}
          <li id="todo-{t's id}">{t's text}</li>
        {else:}
          <li class="empty">Nothing to do.</li>
        {end}
      </ul>
      <p id="status">{if exhausted:}no more todos{end}</p>
    </main>

Style:
    h1 { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: .6rem; }
    h1 small { font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); }
    .error { color: var(--danger); font-weight: 600; }
    .todos { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    .empty { color: var(--muted); padding: .45rem 0; }

## Test: the first page loads on mount

Given that GET "/api/todos?page=1" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 1, \"text\": \"milk\", \"done\": false}}]".
Expect that the count of ".todos li" is equal to 1.
Expect that the text of "#todo-1" is equal to "milk".
Expect that the text of "#count" is equal to "(1)".

## Test: scrolling to the bottom loads the next page and appends it

Given that GET "/api/todos?page=1" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 1, \"text\": \"milk\", \"done\": false}}]".
Given that GET "/api/todos?page=2" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 2, \"text\": \"bread\", \"done\": false}}]".
Raise "scrolledtobottom".
Expect that the count of ".todos li" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#todo-2" is equal to "bread".
Expect that the text of "#count" is equal to "(2)".

## Test: an empty page marks the feed exhausted and stops further loads

Given that GET "/api/todos?page=1" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 1, \"text\": \"milk\", \"done\": false}}]".
Given that GET "/api/todos?page=2" answers 200 with "[]".
Given that GET "/api/todos?page=3" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 3, \"text\": \"eggs\", \"done\": false}}]".
Raise "scrolledtobottom".
Expect that the text of "#status" is equal to "no more todos".
Raise "scrolledtobottom".
Expect that the count of ".todos li" is equal to 1.
Expect that the text of "#count" is equal to "(1)".

## Test: a failed page shows what went wrong and stops loading

Given that GET "/api/todos?page=1" answers 503 with "feed offline".
Expect that the text of ".error" is equal to "503: feed offline".
Expect that the text of "#status" is equal to "no more todos".
Expect that the text of ".empty" is equal to "Nothing to do.".
